  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 85,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "The two-piece donation engine is SPLIT ACROSS TWO CITIES: Howling Mine, Kami of the Crescent Moon and the three upkeep punishers (Iron Maiden, Ebony Owl Netsuke, Viseling) sit in city-2's SET AND FORGET, while the rest of the give-and-charge machine sits in city-3. The split tracks cost and card type, not function — membership reads right, but anyone tracing the engine has to read both cities.",
      "city-2-hood-1 is the most far-flung thing on the map: two cards (the Medallions) at cx -0.98 while their city's centroid is -0.15. They are unusual for this deck's space, not misplaced — per-spell cost reduction is the commander's own back-face text, so they are the only cards that stack with the deck's central asymmetry.",
      "Mikokoro, Center of the Sea is an eleventh table-draw engine filed in the land city. The map is right that it is mana; the reader should know the giveaway count under GIVE THEN CHARGE understates by one because one of those effects is a land.",
      "An Offer You Can't Refuse is the odd member of city-4 — a counterspell clustered with mana rocks, almost certainly on 'creates two Treasure tokens'. Functionally it belongs with THE HARD NO. Not a membership complaint: the ability space weighed the treasure clause over the counter clause, and Smothering Tithe next door makes the same treasure off the same donated draws.",
      "city-3-hood-2 is the thinnest split on the map: three cards whose jobs genuinely differ (donate, break an artifact, untap lands). The label names the only shared shape I can see — permanents that arrive and keep working — rather than pretending the cluster has a single function.",
      "city-0 and city-4 each contain exactly one neighbourhood identical to the parent city. Nothing narrower to say, so both are omitted and the deterministic word stands.",
      "city-5 carries 4 of the map's 10 verified cards on 9 cards — the densest verified block. city-1 (18 lands) carries none, which is expected and not a gap."
    ]
  },
